{
  "title": "Cache out of memory after API deploy",
  "alert": "Product pages load slowly or show 'Service unavailable' errors; the issue comes and goes every few minutes.",
  "truth": {
    "service": "cache",
    "category": "memory",
    "root_cause": "The api 2.3.1 deploy changed the caching layer to store full product JSON blobs instead of only IDs. Over three days this grew Redis past its 256 MiB limit, so the container is repeatedly OOM-killed (signal 9) and restarts.",
    "fix": "Roll back api to 2.3.0 (or disable the new caching behaviour), then verify Redis stays up. Long term: either give Redis more memory or change the API to cache smaller values."
  },
